CONTRACT ANALYSIS: SSE2 is baseline x86-64 (subset of v3; no new
ISA, no capability gating needed). Integer code: no FP state, no
MXCSR/DE/DAZ/FTZ/unmasked-exception surface (unlike roundsd work).
Same return value (dst), no errno, no ABI change, forward path
object-code-identical. Upstream offers a GPR-only variant (~2x
slower); NOT recommended — SSE2 is baseline, keep the fast form.
Disassembly proof: zero std/cld/rep in the candidate backward path.

